---
import { SITE_AUTHOR } from '../consts';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { url } from '../utils/urls';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Compost et Coagula, an independent publication of essays, research notes, and work in progress.">
	<article class="about">
		<header class="page-header">
			<h1>About</h1>
		</header>
		<div class="prose">
			<p>
				Compost et Coagula is the independent publication of {SITE_AUTHOR.name}: a place for essays, research notes, and intellectual work in
				progress. I write across theology, environmental science, history, literature, and software, following questions that rarely remain confined to one discipline.
			</p>
			<p>
				The subjects that recur here include Christian theology and the philosophy of religion; soil science, ecology, and geomorphology;
				environmental and social history; literature and literary criticism; intellectual history and philosophy; and the design of software
				for reading and research.
			</p>
			<p>
				The publication is independent and interdisciplinary. It is not affiliated with any institution or church, and nothing here should
				be read as an official or settled position. Essays are arguments made as carefully as I can make them; working notes are provisional
				by design. When a piece changes in a way that matters to its argument, the revision is noted on the page.
			</p>

			<h2>Projects</h2>
			<p>
				Much of the writing belongs to longer projects. The principal one is
				<a href={url('/projects/the-cruciform-ground/')}>The Cruciform Ground</a>, a place-based theological inquiry centered on Oak Ridge,
				Tennessee. Notes on <a href={url('/projects/deftere/')}>Deftere</a>, a research and learning assistant, appear here as development
				journals.
			</p>

			<h2>The name</h2>
			<p>
				The name began as a playful adaptation of the old formula <i lang="la">solve et coagula</i>, by way of soil science: organic matter
				breaks down, and from that breakdown new structure forms.
			</p>

			{/*
				EDITABLE PLACEHOLDER — not rendered on the site.
				The author's name comes from SITE_AUTHOR in src/consts.ts. Add a sentence
				or two of biography and a contact method here if you want them. Keep it to details
				you are comfortable publishing.
			*/}

			<h2>Following along</h2>
			<p>New writing is listed on the <a href={url('/writing/')}>writing page</a> and in the <a href={url('/rss.xml')}>RSS feed</a>.</p>
		</div>
	</article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.about {
		max-width: var(--measure);
		margin-inline: auto;
	}
</style>
